        <item>
            <title>3.16.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:28:29 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>187</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.16.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features
- **Ask a session from Slack.** A session can be connected to a Slack thread from the pane menu (Connect to Slack Thread…). People in the thread mention @Saqoolaude to ask it questions; each answer reaches the thread only after you approve the draft in your Slack DM. The first question from each person asks you for permission first.
  - While answering from Slack, the session can only read files inside its own folder. Every other tool (shell, edits, web, MCP) is refused, credential-like files are refused, and `@path` mentions in the question cannot attach files.
  - Off by default. Turn it on for one Mac with `"canopy.slackBridgeEnabled": true` in settings.json.
- `canopyctl send --slack-asker` and the `slack_bind` / `slack_unbind` / `slack_bindings` control verbs.

### Bug Fixes
- "View output logs" shows the extension's output-channel logs again.
]]></description>
